@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
@accessToken = replace-with-jwt-access-token
@personId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@person2Id = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@householdId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@signalTypeId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@assessmentTypeId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### --- W2-S1: Person, Phones, Search Keys, Metaphones & Fast Search ---

### Create a person with normalized E.164 phone
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/crm/people
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Robert",
  "nickName": "Bob",
  "lastName": "Decker",
  "gender": "Male",
  "maritalStatus": "Married",
  "birthYear": 1984,
  "birthMonth": 4,
  "birthDay": 15,
  "email": "bob.decker@example.org",
  "connectionStatus": "Member",
  "phoneNumbers": [
    {
      "numberType": "Mobile",
      "number": "(602) 555-0199",
      "isMessagingEnabled": true
    }
  ]
}

### Search people (pg_trgm, phonetic, nickname, phone suffix, search key)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/crm/people/search?query=Rob%20Decker&maxResults=25
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Get Person 360 profile (automatically follows merge redirects)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/crm/people/{{personId}}?followRedirects=true
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Inspect meta first-name gender prediction, nicknames & Double Metaphone keys
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/crm/people/meta/name-insights?firstName=Elizabeth
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Add alternate search key (barcode)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/crm/people/{{personId}}/search-keys
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "personId": "{{personId}}",
  "keyType": "Barcode",
  "searchValue": "CHK-88421"
}

### --- W2-S2: Households & Apache AGE Relationship Graph ---

### Create a household with members
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/crm/households
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Decker Household",
  "combineContributionsByDefault": true,
  "members": [
    {
      "personId": "{{personId}}",
      "role": "Adult",
      "householdOrder": 0,
      "isCombinedContributionMember": true,
      "isPrimaryContact": true
    }
  ]
}

### List households for a person
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/crm/households/by-person/{{personId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Add a known relationship (creates reciprocal inverse + syncs Apache AGE)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/crm/relationships/known
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ownerPersonId": "{{personId}}",
  "relatedPersonId": "{{person2Id}}",
  "relationshipType": "CanCheckIn",
  "notes": "Authorized family friend"
}

### Upsert a peer-network edge
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/crm/relationships/peer-network
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourcePersonId": "{{personId}}",
  "targetPersonId": "{{person2Id}}",
  "relationshipType": "Following",
  "strength": "Casual",
  "caption": "Following",
  "relationshipStartDate": "2026-01-01"
}

### Traverse Apache AGE crm_graph (multi-hop)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/crm/relationships/graph/{{personId}}?maxHops=2
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### --- W2-S3: Duplicate Detection, Redirects & Person Merge ---

### Trigger duplicate scan
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/crm/duplicates/scan
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### List candidate duplicates
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/crm/duplicates?minConfidenceScore=40
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Merge retired person into surviving person
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/crm/duplicates/merge
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "survivingPersonId": "{{personId}}",
  "retiredPersonId": "{{person2Id}}",
  "hasElevatedMergeAuthorization": true
}

### Resolve canonical PersonId via PersonRedirectLedger
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/crm/duplicates/redirects/{{person2Id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### --- W2-S4: Signals, Badges, Assessments, Background Checks & Verification ---

### Create a SignalType
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/crm/signals/types
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Allergy Alert",
  "signalColor": "#D13438",
  "signalIcon": "warning",
  "order": 1
}

### Attach a signal to a person (recalculates TopSignal)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/crm/signals/person
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "personId": "{{personId}}",
  "signalTypeId": "{{signalTypeId}}",
  "ownerPersonId": "{{personId}}",
  "note": "Severe peanut allergy"
}

### Evaluate modular badges for a person
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/crm/badges/person/{{personId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### List assessment types
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/crm/assessments/types?activeOnly=true
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Request an assessment
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/crm/assessments/request
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "personId": "{{personId}}",
  "assessmentTypeId": "{{assessmentTypeId}}"
}

### List background check provider packages
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/crm/background-checks/packages
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Request a background check
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/crm/background-checks/request
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "personId": "{{personId}}",
  "providerKey": "in-memory",
  "packageName": "standard-volunteer"
}

### Issue an identity verification challenge
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/crm/identity-verifications/issue
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "referenceNumber": "+16025550199",
  "requestIpAddress": "127.0.0.1"
}

### Record a PersonViewed audit entry
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/crm/person-viewed
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "targetPersonId": "{{personId}}",
  "source": "Ruth.Host"
}
